      "message": "You\u0027re correct.  The assertion is that as it\u0027s a library that is \u0027additive\u0027 only *and* only contains constant strings (no code/functaional changes/bugs) the likelihood of it causing a regression is low (but I guess non-zero).\n\nA project may specify a minimum version, but there is no reason for it to add a maximum version, so from a distro POV just pick the \"highest minimum\"?\n\nI\u0027m fine with this exception, but I don\u0027t really see a \"great advantage\" to it.\n\n#shrug",
